<title>USA: High cotton prices trigger import quota - USDA.</title>
<headline>High cotton prices trigger import quota - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>High cotton prices have triggered another special quota permitting entry of 44,607,955 kilograms (98,343,787 lbs), the U.S. Department of Agriculture said Thursday.</p>
<p>The quota, being established on Nov 13, 1997, applies to cotton purchased not later than Feb 10, 1997 and entered into the United States not later than May 11, 1997, USDA said.</p>
